ref5("36001662","invitro",M,["induction","effectors"],"th","Irradiated osteoblasts screened over PEMF intensities and frequencies (5-100 Hz): a burst waveform at 15 Hz and 2 mT (carrier 4.55 kHz, 0.2 ms pulses, 7.5% duty) gave the most prominent Ca2+ oscillations/spikes versus other waveforms, intensities and frequencies; primary cilia/polycystin-1/2 and ER were required, and PEMF protected rat bone from radiation loss. Osteocyte-like MLO-Y4 cells did not respond.")
ref5("30774471","human",M,["induction"],"+","Audit of 1,382 nonunion patients using a 15 Hz burst device (4.5 ms bursts, 18 G = 1.8 mT peak per 225 us pulse, 10 h/day recommended): 89.6% reported healed; each extra daily hour cut time to heal by about 6-9 days, patients using it more than 9 h/day healed about 76 days sooner than those using it 3 h or less, with no further gain above about 10 h/day (observational audit with recorded device-use times).")
