ref5("19274753","invitro",M,["induction","effectors"],"+","Human MSCs given 7.5 Hz repetitive quasi-rectangular 300 us pulses at 0.13 mT rms with a stated induced E of 2 mV/cm showed earlier ALP and Runx2/ALP mRNA rise and a delayed increase in cell number during osteogenic culture.")
ref5("22495854","invitro",M,["induction"],"th","Human MSCs given PEMF at 5, 25, 50, 75, 100 and 150 Hz at 1.1 mT for 30 min/day for 21 days: ALP and osteocalcin differentiation rose from 5 to 50 Hz and declined again from 50 to 150 Hz, peaking at 50 Hz (a frequency peak at fixed B).")
ref5("23775573","invitro",M,["induction"],"th","Rat calvarial osteoblasts exposed to sinusoidal, triangular, square and serrated 50 Hz, 1.8 mT fields: square raised proliferation, sinusoidal lowered it, triangular and sinusoidal gave greater ALP, calcium deposition, Runx2, OPG and IGF-I than square/serrated, with triangular the strongest, so waveform at identical f and B changes the outcome.")
